W: 1. A bold young farmer courted me,
W: He gained my heart and my liberty;
W: He gained my heart with a free good wlll,
W: And I must confess that I love him still.
W:
W: 2. I wish, I wish, but it's all in vain,
W: I wish I was a maid again,
W: But a maid again I never shall be,
W: Since that young farmer lay still with me.
W:
W: 3. I wish my baby little was born,
W: And smiling on its fathers knee;
W: And I, poor girl, was dead and gone,
W: And the green grass growing over me.
W:
W: 4. There is a house in yonder town,
W: Where my love goes and sI1s him down,
W: And takes some strange girl on his knee,
W: And tells her things that he won't tell me.
W:
W: 5. Go dig my grave long, wide, and deep,
W: Put a marble stone at my head and feet,
W: Put over and above a pure white dove,
W: To let the world know that I died for love.
W:
W: 6. There is a bird in yonder tree,
W: Some say he's blind and cannot see,
W: And I wish it had been the same with me,
